w.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50545207/2026-college-football-power-rankings-top-25-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tennessee fined by SEC after fans throw golf balls on field","description":"Tennessee was fined $250,000 by the SEC after fans threw golf balls and mustard bottles onto the football field late during Saturday's win over LSU.","published":"2026-11-23T01:42:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50568028/tennessee-fined-sec-fans-throw-golf-balls-field","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Notre Dame loses safety Luke Talich to torn Achilles","description":"Notre Dame starting safety Luke Talich sustained a torn right Achilles tendon in Saturday's win against SMU, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-22T23:15:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50566676/notre-dame-loses-safety-luke-talich-torn-achilles","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What Week 12's unexpected results mean for Rivalry Week and beyond","description":"After another chaotic weekend, we look at the playoff and conference races on the line with one game to go.","published":"2026-11-22T23:54:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50563018/week-12-results-rivalry-week","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 recruit AJ Randle Jr. flips from Miami to Notre Dame","description":"Notre Dame coach Marcus Freeman flipped Miami pledge AJ Randle Jr., ESPN's No. 9 outside linebacker in the 2027 recruiting class, to fill a late-cycle need.","published":"2026-11-22T22:48:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50565158/2027-recruit-aj-randle-jr-flips-miami-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pac-12 reveals unique flex schedule for season's final week","description":"The Pac-12 announced its unique flex schedule for the final week of the regular season early Sunday morning.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564960/pac-12-reveals-unique-flex-schedule-season-final-week","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Montana State ranked No. 1, 5-7 LIU makes FCS bracket as conference champ","description":"Defending national champion Montana State received the top seed for the 24-team FCS playoffs, while Northeast Conference champion LIU (5-7) became the first playoff team with a losing record since 2017.","published":"2026-11-23T00:02:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564910/montana-state-grabs-top-seed-24-team-fcs-playoff-bracket","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest rewards DC Scottie Hazelton with contract extension","description":"Wake Forest defensive coordinator Scottie Hazelton has signed a contract extension.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564902/wake-forest-rewards-dc-scottie-hazelton-extension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4921108/desean-bishop","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeSean_Bishop"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"DeSean Bishop","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeSean_Bishop","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:30Z","intro":"DeSean Bishop (born October 15, 2004) is an American college football running back for the Tennessee Volunteers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Bishop played running back for Karns High School where he recorded 8,347 rushing yards and 102 rushing touchdowns. On July 14, 2022, Bishop committed to continue his playing career at Coastal Carolina, but decommitted after head coach Jamey Chadwell was hired by Liberty. On December 21, 2022, Bishop decided to join the Tennessee Volunteers as a preferred walk-on."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"During his true freshman year, Bishop did not play in any games and took a redshirt after suffering an injury during the preseason.\nDuring the 2024 season, Bishop served as the second-string running back behind All-SEC selection Dylan Sampson. Despite facing injuries in the later weeks of the season, Bishop was able to accumulate 455 yards and three touchdowns on 74 carries.\nIn January 2025, Bishop was given a football scholarship. He finished the 2025 season with 182 carries for 1,076 rushing yards and 16 rushing touchdowns."}]}}